{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Engine comparison run (antifungal-amenable-mite), recorded 2026-11-12 00:05 PST.\n\nSetup:\n- Harness: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison`, AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock, from a worktree at origin/main 6dbf05538f7 plus the harness commit.\n- Corpus: the frozen replay labels file evals/plan-review-gate/replay/labels-b3784f06….jsonl, all 11 verified whole plans (7 historical PASS, 3 BLOCK, 1 INDETERMINATE); digest c386161d43b1….\n- Each plan was reviewed under both engines in a disposable store seeded with its file_impact files at HEAD, unsigned, with no sidecar.\n\nResults (src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json, valid=true, no errors, floor blocks or INDETERMINATEs on either engine):\n- Verdict agreement: 8/11 (0.73). Confusion matrix (pipeline rows × agentic columns): PASS→PASS 7, PASS→BLOCK 2, BLOCK→BLOCK 1, BLOCK→PASS 1.\n- Blocking flips: 3. The agentic engine blocked 2 plans the pipeline passed, and passed 1 the pipeline blocked.\n- Finding overlap (token-set Jaccard ≥ 0.5, DET excluded): 3 matched, 118 pipeline-only, 56 agentic-only. The pipeline surfaces about 2× as many findings, and they are worded very differently; a Jaccard-on-tokens match undercounts semantic overlap, so treat this as a lower bound.\n- Agreement with the historical pipeline verdict (10 decided rows): pipeline 5/10, agentic 5/10. Today's pipeline already disagrees with its own older verdicts on half these plans.\n\nWall time per plan: about 2–3 min pipeline and about 40–80 s agentic."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794470967134733968,"uuid":"58f81508-9d7c-4e3e-b10d-0de9f1be0ab5"}